{"authored" [{"question" "q-336419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+2t.$ Calculate the acceleration $a$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf987c60cf837c442d97ad351566ec958b4480ce2e6089834228d02a50514b8f" "basis" 1291 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+2t) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{t+1}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf987c60cf837c442d97ad351566ec958b4480ce2e6089834228d02a50514b8f" "basis" 1291 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe66d890c0d20832f8197c4aff0809c957f75deffbbfe81604a7b8ed13ae9c7b" "basis" 1291 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336419" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf987c60cf837c442d97ad351566ec958b4480ce2e6089834228d02a50514b8f" "basis" 1291 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement $s$ of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)={t}^{2}+\\frac{6}{t+2}.$ Find the particle's acceleration at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf987c60cf837c442d97ad351566ec958b4480ce2e6089834228d02a50514b8f" "basis" 1291 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+\\frac{6}{t+2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+6(t+2)^{-1}) \\\\  & =2t-6(t+2)^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-6(t+2)^{-2}) \\\\  & =2+12(t+2)^{-3} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{12}{(t+2)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf987c60cf837c442d97ad351566ec958b4480ce2e6089834228d02a50514b8f" "basis" 1291 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe66d890c0d20832f8197c4aff0809c957f75deffbbfe81604a7b8ed13ae9c7b" "basis" 1291 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf987c60cf837c442d97ad351566ec958b4480ce2e6089834228d02a50514b8f" "basis" 1291 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{12}{(t+2)^3}+2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf987c60cf837c442d97ad351566ec958b4480ce2e6089834228d02a50514b8f" "basis" 1291 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-4772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in centimeters) of an ant moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)={t}^{2}+3t,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds.\nFind the ant's acceleration at $t=10$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-4772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+3t) \\\\  & =2t+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+3) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=10,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\na(10)=2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=10$ seconds is $2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-4772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b8c6d6121f21b46d1a2c14b568879674ab0572bf345fc21af8debb5d96a7a26"} {"question" "q-4772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-4772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10{\\text{ cm/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "15{\\text{ cm/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "2{\\text{ cm/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "4{\\text{ cm/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "8{\\text{ cm/s}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c69