reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b8c6d6121f21b46d1a2c14b568879674ab0572bf345fc21af8debb5d96a7a26"} {"question" "q-336419" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-336419" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{t+1}+2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-336429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)={t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t+1.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and $t>0.$\n\nWhen $a=2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ the velocity is $v=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-336429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t+1) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-6t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=2,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =3{t}^{2}-6t+2 \\\\ 0 & =3{t}^{2}-6t \\\\ 3t(t-2) & =0 \\\\ t & =0,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $t=2$ since $t>0.$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=2,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =(2)^{3}-3(2)^{2}+2(2)+1 \\\\  & =8-12+4+1 \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $v=1\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-336429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b8c6d6121f21b46d1a2c14b568879674ab0572bf345fc21af8debb5d96a7a26"} {"question" "q-336429" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-336429" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement $s$ of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)={t}^{2}+\\frac{6}{t+2}.$ Find the particle's acceleration at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+\\frac{6}{t+2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+6(t+2)^{-1}) \\\\  & =2t-6(t+2)^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-6(t+2)^{-2}) \\\\  & =2+12(t+2)^{-3} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{12}{(t+2)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b8c6d6121f21b46d1a2c14b568879674ab0572bf345fc21af8debb5d96a7a26"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2+\\frac{12}{(t+2)^3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040240/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b2bc1fd72e3682f8ea5f670b3cfd3fbcf7d86b44e72980c6942a47671842612"}] "usage" {"q-336455" [] "q-336419" []} "basis" 1441 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186298250 17592186298251 17592186298262] "immutable_fields" [[17592186298249 :answer-field/correct] [17592186298249 :answer-field/id] [17592186298249 :answer-field/key] [17592186298249 :answer-field/type] [17592186298261 :a